early-170-years-ago-was-rediscovered-in-a-museum-drawer-and-helped-identify-11-new-species/articleshow/135537442.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-moth-collected-by-alfred-russel-wallace-nearly-170-years-ago-was-rediscovered-in-a-museum-drawer-and-helped-identify-11-new-species/articleshow/135537442.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T03:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135537565,imgsize-759358.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arkansas couple win right to complete 111-acre land purchase after years of instalments]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135598180.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Destin and Jennifer Clark faced a legal battle over a land purchase in Magazine, Arkansas. They initially struggled with payments and entered various agreements with the sellers, George and Sandra Thomas. A dispute arose regarding the sellers' refusal to provide a signed payoff amount, which the Clarks needed to finalize the sale. The Arkansas Court of Appeals affirmed the lower court's ruling, allowing the Clarks to complete the purchase.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-an-arkansas-couple-began-buying-111-acres-on-instalments-later-handing-over-a-truck-and-cows-to-catch-up-when-the-seller-resisted-closing-an-appeals-court-upheld-their-right-to-complete-the-sale/articleshow/135598180.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-an-arkansas-couple-began-buying-111-acres-on-instalments-later-handing-over-a-truck-and-cows-to-catch-up-when-the-seller-resisted-closing-an-appeals-court-upheld-their-right-to-complete-the-sale/articleshow/135598180.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T01:48:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135598345,imgsize-2063178.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discovered hundreds of sensory hair cells across squid body, insight into human hearing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135629743.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Research conducted at Case Western Reserve University has uncovered that squids possess sensory hair cells throughout their bodies. These cells grant squids an exceptional ability to perceive local water movements, akin to how humans detect sound through their ears. The variation in hair bundle lengths allows for the discernment of different water motion frequencies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/scientists-discovered-hundreds-of-sensory-hair-cells-across-the-entire-surface-of-squid-bodies-not-just-their-heads-and-arms-the-finding-may-offer-a-new-way-to-study-how-human-hearing-cells-fail/articleshow/135629743.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/scientists-discovered-hundreds-of-sensory-hair-cells-across-the-entire-surface-of-squid-bodies-not-just-their-heads-and-arms-the-finding-may-offer-a-new-way-to-study-how-human-hearing-cells-fail/articleshow/135629743.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135630100,imgsize-71243.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet 15-year-old Rodion Zaichikov, the Luxembourg student who won the Ellison Scholars Prize]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135629543.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At just 15 years old, Rodion Zaichikov has made waves in the scientific community with his innovative arc-jet wind tunnel designed for scramjet testing, which earned him the prestigious Ellison Scholars Prize at Germany's European Union Contest for Young Scientists. By creating equipment to mimic extreme flight conditions—typically costly and hard to access—Zaichikov showcases his dedication to pioneering aerospace solutions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-15-year-old-rodion-zaichikov-the-luxembourg-student-who-built-an-arc-jet-wind-tunnel-to-test-a-scramjet-above-3000c-and-won-the-ellison-scholars-prize-at-europes-young-scientist-contest/articleshow/135629543.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-15-year-old-rodion-zaichikov-the-luxembourg-student-who-built-an-arc-jet-wind-tunnel-to-test-a-scramjet-above-3000c-and-won-the-ellison-scholars-prize-at-europes-young-scientist-contest/articleshow/135629543.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T01:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135629609,imgsize-62128.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Virginia restaurant gets $51,594 water bill after meter fault hid usage for years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135538147.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-virginia-restaurant-received-a-51594-water-bill-after-paying-almost-nothing-for-three-years-a-damaged-meter-transmitter-had-been-recording-zero-consumption/articleshow/135538147.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-virginia-restaurant-received-a-51594-water-bill-after-paying-almost-nothing-for-three-years-a-damaged-meter-transmitter-had-been-recording-zero-consumption/articleshow/135538147.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T02:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135538207,imgsize-1210710.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[10 years of the Paris Agreement, top 10 carbon emitters of the world; where does India stand]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135630304.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Natural disasters have spotlighted the urgent link between climate change and escalating global carbon emissions. The 2025 Global Carbon Budget predicts fossil fuel emissions will soar to unprecedented levels. Although India is among the top three carbon emitters, its per-capita emissions are significantly lower compared to China and the U.S.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/10-years-of-the-paris-agreement-who-are-the-top-10-carbon-emitters-of-the-world-and-where-does-india-stand/articleshow/135630304.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/10-years-of-the-paris-agreement-who-are-the-top-10-carbon-emitters-of-the-world-and-where-does-india-stand/articleshow/135630304.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135630645,imgsize-99335.cms"/></item></channel></rss>